id: pm-2x5x83
title: Tracker-only PM governance commits cannot satisfy required CI without changing the generated changelog
description: "The required static CI lane runs changelog:pm:check against every push. A deliberately tracker-only audit that closes PM items changes the generated changelog input, so exact-head CI fails unless the session also edits CHANGELOG.md, contradicting a valid PM-only/no-docs scope and making direct tracker governance unable to produce a green required-check set."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-workflow,"area:ci",changelog,governance,tracker-only
created_at: "2026-08-04T09:41:11.527Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T09:41:57.367Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Decide and document whether tracker-only closed-item mutations must always regenerate CHANGELOG.md or may be classified outside product changelog inputs; CI, contributor guidance, pm-changelog generation, and auto-release change classification share one explicit contract; a clean fixture proves a tracker-only planning commit can follow that contract without an empty npm/Bun release; a negative control proves a product-visible closed item still fails when its generated changelog is stale; direct-main and PR paths report the same policy; regression evidence references an exact source SHA and generated artifact diff; no manual CHANGELOG edits are introduced"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: GitHub Actions main push at 9d28e08b96b1caa36d41e68ef82e09ebb2e46c78
repro_steps: "Commit only append-only .agents/pm planning and evidence changes that close a PM item; push to main; observe CI run 30897051387 job 91952524714 fail in Run static + secret + version gates because pnpm changelog:pm:check reports CHANGELOG.md out of date."
expected_result: A tracker-only PM governance commit has an explicit policy path that preserves generated changelog ownership and still yields an honest required-check result without requiring an out-of-scope docs mutation or empty product release.
actual_result: "The tracker-only audit commit reached main, but the required CI static job failed solely because CHANGELOG.md was intentionally not regenerated; all preceding version and extension setup steps succeeded."
component: CI and changelog governance
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-gzyt2j,discovered_from,"2026-08-04T09:41:11.527Z","harness:codex","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:41:11.527Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: searched every status for tracker-only commit, changelog out-of-date, generated changelog governance, direct-main, and changelog drag. Existing pm-6san defines generated ownership, pm-pivf owns a specific GH-209 warning cleanup, and pm-u9d0 owns CI/release capability; no active or terminal item owns the general required-check policy conflict reproduced on exact head. This item is the focused canonical owner."
  "2026-08-04T09:41:30.260Z","harness:codex","Hosted evidence: exact-head CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/30897051387, static job https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/actions/runs/30897051387/job/91952524714. The job checked out 9d28e08b96b1caa36d41e68ef82e09ebb2e46c78 and failed with Changelog is out of date after successfully installing pm-changelog 2026.8.4. This audit does not regenerate CHANGELOG.md because the user explicitly limited mutations to PM planning/documentation; the failure is preserved as policy evidence, not repaired in this session."
  "2026-08-04T09:41:57.367Z","harness:codex","Exact-head hosted inventory is complete: Security and Script Quality, OSSF Scorecard, CodSpeed, and CodeQL all succeeded on 9d28e08b96b1caa36d41e68ef82e09ebb2e46c78. CI completed with 13 successful jobs and exactly one failed job, Gates (static) 91952524714; the failing step was changelog:pm:check reporting only that CHANGELOG.md was out of date. This isolates the policy conflict from product build, typecheck, compatibility, smoke, coverage, Windows, benchmark, and security outcomes."
